## Nomenclature

Some nomenclature that can be of help:

- `SPC`: Space key.
- `ESC`: Escape key.
- `C`: Control key.
- `M`: Meta key (Alt, Option).
- `s`: Super (Windows)

If a letter is uppercase, it implies the use of the _Shift_ key.

The different key combinations can be seen as
a sequence of keys, or a chord or musical arpeggio.

### Arpeggios

Similar to an arpeggio are the key combinations that
must be pressed in a sequential order.

They can be identified when a `space` is used to separate the key sequence.

Example: `SPC f P` means:

1. Press `Space` and release.
2. Press `f` and release.
3. Press `P` (uppercase) and release.

### Chords

Similar to a chord. They are a set of keys
that must be pressed at the same time (without releasing the previous one).

They can be identified when a `-` is used to separate the key sequence.

Example: `C-x` means:

1. Press `Control` and keep holding.
2. Press `x` and then release all the keys (`Control`, `x`) at the same time.

## Special Configurations

The following configurations must be done in the
`config.el` file available at `~/.config/doom/config.el`.

To access this configuration from _Emacs_ you simply
press the key combination

```text
SPC f-P
```

### Configure Options

Edit the `config.el` file and add the following `lisp` instructions.

```clojure
;; User Info
(setq user-full-name "Camilo Castro"
      user-mail-address "camilo@ninjas.cl")

;; Mac Config
(setq mac-option-modifier 'alt
      mac-pass-control-to-system nil)

;; Ctrl+K removes whole line
(setq kill-whole-line t)

;; Enable auto save and backup files
(setq auto-save-default t
      make-backup-files t)

;; Disable confirm on exit
(setq confirm-kill-emacs nil)

;; Set Fonts
(setq doom-font (font-spec :family "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font" :size 16))

;; Set Window Size
(setq initial-frame-alist '((top . 1) (left . 1) (width . 143) (height . 55)))
```


### Change the Logo

Let's change the startup screen for a more polished one.

The following is what we get out of the box when installing _Doom Emacs_.

![Startup Screen](inicio.png)

And we are going to add a nicer one (Made by Zzamboni)

![Doom](doom.png)

## Copy the Image

Let's copy the image to the corresponding directory

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/doom/splash
cp doom-emacs-bw-light.svg ~/.config/doom/splash
```

We edit `config.el` and add the following `lisp` instructions.

```clojure
(let ((images '("doom-emacs-bw-light.svg")))
  (setq fancy-splash-image
        (concat doom-user-dir "splash/"
                (nth (random (length images)) images))))
```


Finally we will have a nice result.

![Emacs](emacs.png)


